// Occupations and roles of Named characters (DEC-018, DEC-031): the people
// worth remembering who are not politicians. Each town gets them at its
// places (`places`: place kinds, or `streets` for one per neighbourhood),
// with `chance` per place. `leader`s head an organisation: they are Principal
// characters and can be a town's power broker, weighted by `influence` and by
// their `stake` (sector drivers and crisis kinds they speak for). `class`
// weighs the income classes they come from ([low, middle, high]); their
// values start from that cohort of their home neighbourhood, plus noise.
// `personality` and `competencies` are offsets. `ambient` occupations may
// also be passers-by (Ambient people, generated on demand and never stored).
// Registry order is load order.
